
### ######################## GATEWAY DEMO ########################

### 1) Check product availability through Order Service
GET http://localhost:7070/orders/inventory/3
Content-Type: application/json
X-Client-Id: shirin


### 2) Create an order and reserve inventory
POST http://localhost:7070/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Client-Id: shirin

{
  "requestId": "req-001",
  "productId": 1001,
  "quantity": 5
}


### 3) Get inventory directly through Gateway
GET http://localhost:7070/inventory/3
Content-Type: application/json
X-Client-Id: shirin


### 4) Reserve inventory directly through Gateway
POST http://localhost:7070/inventory/reservations
Content-Type: application/json
X-Client-Id: shirin

{
  "requestId": "req-002",
  "productId": 1001,
  "quantity": 5
}


### 5) Programmatic RouteLocator example
GET http://localhost:7070/check/3


### 6) Missing rate-limit key
### Expected: rejected because X-Client-Id is missing
GET http://localhost:7070/inventory/3


### 7) Redis rate limiter
### Run repeatedly with the same client ID.
### Successful responses contain X-RateLimit-* headers.
### When the bucket is exhausted: HTTP 429.
GET http://localhost:7070/inventory/3
X-Client-Id: rate-limit-test
